summary:
  When the cover's menu shuts, the focus goes to the menu's button,
  whoever had it before.

history:
  Seen on the panel on 2026-11-12: a click on the menu's button, one more
  to shut the menu, and Space opened the menu again; the Space after that
  opened Last.fm in the browser. The listener had pressed it to pause. The
  focus returns to where it was before the menu opened. This mutant gives
  it to the button.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CoverTouch.qml

find:
          if (to && to.visible && to.enabled) to.forceActiveFocus()
          else _toFace(from)

replace:
          if (linksButton.visible) linksButton.forceActiveFocus()
          else _toFace(from)

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_space_after_a_click_on_the_cover_is_still_the_pages,
  which runs first and pins the line, and behind it by
  tests/qml/tst_covertouch.qml::test_space_after_the_menu_was_clicked_open_and_shut_is_the_pages,
  which presses the keys.
  Line-neutral.
